# Push Rules

## CRITICAL: Never Push to Master

**NEVER push to master branch unless explicitly asked by the user.**

### Rules:
- Always work on feature/staging branches
- Only push to master when user explicitly requests it
- Ask for confirmation before any master push
- Use `git push origin <branch-name>` instead of `git push` when on master

### Safe Push Commands:
```bash
# Push current branch (safe)
git push origin HEAD

# Push specific branch (safe)
git push origin staging

# Push to master (REQUIRES EXPLICIT USER PERMISSION)
git push origin master
```

### Workflow:
1. Work on staging/feature branches
2. Test changes thoroughly
3. Ask user for explicit permission before master push
4. Only then push to master

This prevents accidental production deployments.